hadiths[119]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18314","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, he said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and he was asked: Did anyone of this nation lead the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in prayer other than Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, and he said: Yes, we were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and when it was before dawn he struck the neck of my mount, and I thought he had a need, so I turned aside with him, and we went on until we were clear of the people, then he dismounted from his mount, then he went off and disappeared from me until I could not see him, and he stayed a long time, then he came and said: Your need, O Mughirah, I said: I have no need, and he said: Have you water with you, and I said: Yes, so I went to a waterskin, or to a flat skin hung at the end of the saddle, and I brought him water, and I poured upon him, and he washed his hands and washed them well, he said: And I doubt whether he said: He rubbed them with dust or not, then he washed his face, then he went to bare his arms, and upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, and it was tight, so he took out his hands from underneath it, and he washed his face and his hands, he said: And there comes in the hadith washing of the face twice, he said: I do not know whether it was so or not, then he wiped his forelock and wiped over the turban and wiped over the two leather socks, and we mounted and caught up with the people while the prayer had been established, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf had gone forward leading them, and he had prayed one rakah with them while they were in the second, and I went to inform him, and he forbade me, so we prayed the rakah we caught, and we made up the rakah we had missed."
"18315","Ya'la ibn Ubayd Abu Yusuf narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will remain of my nation a people dominant over the people until the command of Allah comes to them while they are dominant."
"18316","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Hisham narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he narrated from Ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from Umar, that he consulted them concerning the miscarriage of the woman, so al-Mughirah said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged concerning it with a ghurrah, so Umar said to him: If you are truthful, then bring someone who knows that, so Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged with it."
"18317","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I mentioned to him a woman I was proposing to, and he said: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you, he said: So I went to a woman of the Ansar and proposed to her to her parents, and I told them the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was as if they disliked that, he said: So the woman heard that while she was in her private chamber, and she said: If the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded you to look, then look, otherwise I adjure you, as if she regarded that gravely for him, he said: So I looked at her and I married her, and he mentioned her suitability."
"18318","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that two women, one of them struck the other with a tent pole and killed her, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged the blood money upon the clan of the killer, and for what was in her womb a ghurrah, the bedouin said: Do you make me pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out and gave the birth cry, the like of that is void, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins, and for what is in her womb a ghurrah."
"18319","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah informed me that Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, informed him that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wrote to Muawiyah, Warrad wrote that letter for him: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying when he gives the greeting of peace: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, O Allah, none prevents what You give, and none gives what You prevent, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against You, Warrad said: Then I came as a delegate after that to Muawiyah, and I heard him on the pulpit ordering the people with that saying and teaching it to them."
"18320","Quran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd al-Tai, from Ali ibn Rabiah al-Asadi, he said: A man of the Ansar called Qarazah ibn Ka'b died, and wailing was done over him, so al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah went out and ascended the pulpit, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, he said: What is with wailing in Islam, indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Lying upon me is not like lying upon anyone, indeed whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"18321","Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever is wailed over is punished for what is wailed over him."
"18322","Abdah ibn Sulayman Abu Muhammad al-Kilabi narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I performed ablution for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he washed his face and his forearms and wiped his head and wiped over his two leather socks, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not remove your two leather socks, he said: No, indeed I put them on while they were both pure, then I have not walked barefoot after, then he prayed the dawn prayer."
"18323","Abd al-Muta'al ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, al-Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, he said: The sun eclipsed in the forenoon until its darkness became intense, so al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah stood and prayed with the people, and he stood the length of reading a surah of the oft-repeated ones, then he bowed the like of that, then he raised his head, then he bowed the like of that, then he raised his head, then he stood the like of that, then he bowed the second time the like of that, then the sun cleared, so he prostrated, then he stood the length of reading a surah, then he bowed and prostrated, then he finished, then he ascended the pulpit and said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone, rather they are two signs of the signs of Allah, mighty and majestic, so when one of them eclipses, hasten to prayer, then he came down, and he narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in prayer and began blowing in front of him, then he extended his hand as if reaching for something, and when he finished he said: The Fire was brought near to me until I blew its heat away from my face, and I saw in it the owner of the staff, and the one who dedicated the Bahirah, and the Himyarite woman, the owner of the cat."
"18324","Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, al-Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, the like of it."
"18325","Abu al-Nadr al-Harith ibn al-Nu'man narrated to me, from Shayban, from Jabir, from Amir, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged concerning the two Hudhali women that the bloodwit is upon the clan, and that the inheritance is for the heirs, and that for the fetus is a ghurrah."
"18326","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Bukayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to us that he traveled with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a valley and relieved himself, then he came out, and he came to him and performed ablution, and he removed his two leather socks and performed ablution, and when he finished he found wind after that, so he returned and went out and performed ablution and wiped over his two leather socks, so I said: O Prophet of Allah, you forgot, you did not remove the leather socks, he said: No, rather you forgot, with this my Lord, mighty and majestic, commanded me."
"18327","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: I had memorized from many of our scholars in Madinah that Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm used to narrate from al-Mughirah hadiths, among them that he narrated to him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath."
"18328","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah disliked for you three things: gossip, and excessive asking, and wasting wealth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade you burying daughters alive, and disobedience to mothers, and withholding and demanding."
"18329","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that a woman was struck by a woman with a tent pole and she killed her while she was pregnant, and she was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged concerning her upon the clan of the killer with the blood money, and for the fetus a ghurrah, so her clan said: Do we pay for one who neither tasted nor drank nor cried out and gave the birth cry, the like of that is void, so he said: Rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins, and Shu'bah said: I heard Ubayd."
"18330","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Mansur informed me, he said: I heard Ibrahim narrating from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that two women were under one man, and they became jealous, and she struck her with a tent pole and killed her, and they disputed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out and gave the birth cry, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins, he said: So he judged concerning it a ghurrah, he said: And he placed it upon the female relatives responsible for blood money of the woman."
"18331","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah and Hammad informed us, from Abu Wail, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a refuse heap of the sons of so-and-so and urinated standing, Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman said: So he spread his legs."
"18332","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taking hold of the waist wrapper of Sufyan ibn Abi Sahl, while he was saying: O Sufyan ibn Abi Sahl, do not let your lower garment hang, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang."
"18333","Waki narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Nawfal narrated to me, from a man of the children of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mutilation."
"18334","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he accompanied a party of polytheists and found heedlessness among them, so he killed them and took their wealth, and he brought it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, refused to accept it."
"18335","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I proposed to a woman, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Did you look at her, I said: No, he said: Then look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you."
"18336","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I proposed to a woman, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Did you look at her, I said: No, he said: Then look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you."
"18337","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: No one asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more than I asked him about it, and he said: It will not harm you, he said: I said: They say with him is a river and such and such, he said: He is more insignificant before Allah than that."
"18338","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the backs of the two leather socks."
"18339","Surayj and al-Hashimi also narrated it to us."
"18340","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, he said: I heard Bakr ibn Abdullah narrating from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he said: Two traits I do not ask anyone of the people about, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, doing them: The prayer of the imam behind a man of his subjects, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying behind Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf one rakah of the dawn prayer, and the wiping of a man over his two leather socks, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two leather socks."
"18341","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Abu Said informed me, he said: Warrad, secretary of al-Mughirah, informed me, he said: Muawiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: When he prayed and finished he said: There is no god but Allah, he said, and I think he said: Alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, O Allah, none prevents what You give, and none gives what You prevent, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against You."
"18342","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he relieved himself, then I came to him with a small water vessel, and upon him was a Syrian cloak, he said: And he could not take out his hands from its sleeves, so he took out his hands from beneath it, then he performed ablution and wiped over his two leather socks."
"18343","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Ziyad, from a son of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went for his need in the expedition of Tabuk, al-Mughirah said: So I went with him with water, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and I poured water upon him, and he washed his face, then he went to take out his hands from the sleeves of his cloak and could not because of the narrowness of the sleeves of the cloak, so he took them out from under his cloak, and he washed his hands and wiped his head and wiped over the two leather socks, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading them, and he had prayed one rakah with them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them the remaining rakah upon them, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he said: You did well."
"18344","Abdullah narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Ziyad, of the children of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and he mentioned this hadith, Musab said: And Malik made in it a grave mistake."
"18345","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, Said ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The rider is behind the funeral, and the walker is where he wishes of it, and the child is prayed over."
"18346","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah prayed with us, and when he had prayed two rakahs he stood and did not sit, so those behind him glorified Allah, and he motioned to them to stand, and when he finished his prayer he gave the greeting, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did with us."
"18347","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, he said: I entered the congregational mosque, and Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi had entered from the other side, and we met near the middle of the mosque, and he began speaking to me, and he loved the good he conveyed to me, so he began speaking to me and said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and what he brought the hadith near with increased belief in him in myself, he said: We said: Did a man of this nation lead the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in prayer other than Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, he said: Yes, we were on such-and-such a journey, and when it was before dawn the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck the neck of his mount and went off, and I followed him, and he disappeared from me for an hour, then he came and said: Your need, and I said: I have no need, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Is there water, I said: Yes, so I poured upon him, and he washed his hands, then he washed his face, then he went to bare his forearms, and upon him was a Syrian cloak of his, and it was tight, so he put his hands in and took them out from under the cloak, and he washed his face and washed his forearms and wiped his forelock and wiped over the turban and over the two leather socks, then we caught up with the people while the prayer had been established, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading them, and he had prayed one rakah, so I went to inform him, and he forbade me, so we prayed what we caught, and we made up what we had been preceded in."
"18348","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: A man narrated to me, from Amr ibn Wahb, meaning he mentioned similar to it."
"18349","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There will remain people of my nation fighting upon the truth, dominant, until the command of Allah, mighty and majestic, comes to them."
"18350","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: No one asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the Dajjal more than I asked him about him, so he said to me: O my son, what troubles you from him, indeed he will not harm you, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim that with him are mountains of bread and rivers of water, so he said: He is more insignificant before Allah, mighty and majestic, than that."
"18351","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Warrad, secretary of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah said: If I saw a man with my wife I would strike him with the sword without turning it flat, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Do you wonder at the jealousy of Sad, by Allah, indeed I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than me, and because of the jealousy of Allah He forbade shameful deeds, what is apparent of them and what is hidden, and no person is more jealous than Allah, and no person is more loving of excuse than Allah, for that reason Allah sent the messengers as bearers of glad tidings and warners, and no person is more loving of praise than Allah, for that reason Allah promised Paradise."
"18352","Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it exactly."
"18353","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri said: There is no hadith harder upon the Jahmiyyah than this hadith, his saying: No person is more loving of praise than Allah, mighty and majestic."
"18354","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Iyad narrating from Qabisah ibn Burmah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in some of what he used to travel, and we journeyed until when we were toward dawn he went off until he disappeared from me, and he relieved himself, then he came and called for purifying water, and upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, so he put his hand in from beneath the cloak, then he washed his face and his hands and wiped his head and wiped over the two leather socks."
"18355","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in some of his journeys, and when he went he went far in going, so he went for his need, and he said: O Mughirah, follow me with water, and he mentioned the hadith."
"18356","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed behind and relieved himself, and he said: Have you purifying water with you, he said: So I followed him with a water vessel containing water, and he washed his hands and his face, then he went to bare his forearms, and the sleeves of the cloak were tight, so he took out his hands from under the cloak, and he washed his forearms, then he wiped over his turban and his two leather socks, and he mounted and I mounted my mount, and we reached the people while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf had prayed one rakah with them, and when he sensed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he went to step back, so he motioned to him to complete the prayer, and he said: You did well, do so."
"18357","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he stood in the first two rakahs, and they glorified Allah for him, and he did not sit, and when he finished his prayer he prostrated two prostrations after the greeting, then he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did."
"18358","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Jubayr informed me, my father informed me, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The rider is behind the funeral, and the walker is in front of it, near, on its right or on its left, and the miscarried fetus is prayed over, and supplication is made for its parents for forgiveness and mercy."
"18359","Sad and Ya'qub narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Abbad ibn Ziyad narrated to me, Sad said: Abu Sufyan, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he said: I stayed behind with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Tabuk, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to relieve himself, then he returned to me, and with me was the water vessel, he said: So I poured upon the hands of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he blew his nose, Ya'qub said: Then he rinsed his mouth, then he washed his face three times, then he wanted to wash his hands before taking them out of the sleeves of his cloak, and its sleeves were tight upon him, so he took his hand out of the cloak, and he washed his right hand three times and his left hand three times, and he wiped with his two leather socks and did not remove them, then he headed to the people and found them having put Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf forward praying with them, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, caught one of the two rakahs, and he prayed with the people the last rakah with the prayer of Abd al-Rahman, and when Abd al-Rahman gave the greeting, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood completing his prayer, and that alarmed the Muslims and they increased glorification, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he turned to them and said: You did well and you were right, congratulating them that they prayed the prayer at its time."
"18360","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: And he found from me the smell of garlic, and he said: Who ate garlic, he said: So I took his hand and put it in, and he found my chest bound, he said: Indeed you have an excuse."
"18361","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, in meaning, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, Zayd said: al-Khuzai, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that two co-wives, one of them struck the other with a tent pole and killed her, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged the blood money upon the clan of the killer, and for what was in her womb a ghurrah, the bedouin said: Do you make me pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out and gave the birth cry, then the like of that is void, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins, and for what is in her womb a ghurrah."
"18362","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day Ibrahim died, so the people said: It eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sun and the moon are two signs of the signs of Allah, they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see it, call upon Allah and pray until it clears."
"18363","Ismail narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Ibn Ashwa' narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The secretary of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: Muawiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed Allah disliked for you gossip, and wasting wealth, and excessive asking."
"18364","Ismail narrated to us, Layth informed us, from Mujahid, from al-Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever is cauterized or seeks incantation has quit reliance."
"18365","Ismail narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from his father, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: The rider goes behind the funeral, and the walker walks behind it and in front of it and to its right and to its left, near, and the miscarried fetus is prayed over, supplication is made for its parents for well-being and mercy, Yunus said: And the family of Ziyad mention the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and as for me, I do not remember it."
"18366","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi, he said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and he was asked: Did anyone of this nation lead the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, other than Abu Bakr, he said: Yes, he said: So what he brought the hadith near with increased belief in him in my view, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and when it was before dawn he struck the heel of my mount, and I thought he had a need, so I turned aside with him, and we went on until we were clear of the people, then he dismounted from his mount, then he went off and disappeared from me until I could not see him, and he stayed a long time, then he came and said: Your need, O Mughirah, I said: I have no need, so he said: Have you water with you, I said: Yes, so I went to a waterskin, or he said: A flat skin hung at the end of the saddle, and I brought it to him, and I poured upon him, and he washed his hands and washed them well, he said: And I doubt whether he said: He rubbed them with dust or not, then he washed his face, then he went to bare his arm, and upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, and it was tight, so he took out his hands from underneath it, and he washed his face and his hands, he said: And there comes in the hadith washing of the face twice, and I do not know whether it was so or not, then he wiped his forelock and wiped over the turban and wiped over the two leather socks, then we mounted and caught up with the people while the prayer had been established, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf had gone forward leading them, and he had prayed one rakah with them while they were in the second, and I went to inform him, and he forbade me, so we prayed the rakah we caught, and we made up what we had been preceded in."
"18367","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi narrating from Warrad, secretary of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that al-Mughirah wrote to Muawiyah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he gave the greeting of peace said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, O Allah, none prevents what You give, and none gives what You prevent, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against You."
"18368","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, Ibn Jafar said: I heard Maymun ibn Abi Shabib narrating from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever narrates from me a hadith while seeing it is a lie, he is one of the liars."
"18369","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: We used to pray with the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the noon prayer in the midday heat, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: Cool the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"18370","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taking hold of the waist wrapper of Sufyan ibn Abi Sahl, and he said: O Sufyan ibn Abi Sahl, do not let your lower garment hang, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang."
"18371","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Malik, from Husayn ibn Uqbah, from al-Mughirah."
"18372","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Qabisah ibn Jabir, from al-Mughirah."
"18373","Abu al-Nadr said: From Husayn, from al-Mughirah."
"18374","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he said to me: O Mughirah, take the water vessel, he said: So I took it, he said: Then I went with him, and he went on until he disappeared from me, and he relieved himself, then he came, and upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, he said: So he went to take out his hands from it, and it was tight, so he took out his hands from beneath the cloak, and I poured upon him, and he performed ablution, his ablution for prayer, then he wiped his two leather socks, then he prayed."
"18375","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ibn Sawqah, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: Muawiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with no one between you and him, he said: So he dictated to me, and I wrote: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed Allah forbade three things and prohibited three things, as for the three that Allah prohibited: gossip, and persistent asking, and wasting wealth."
"18376","Hushaim narrated to us, more than one informed us, among them Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, secretary of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Muawiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: So al-Mughirah wrote to him: I heard him saying at the end of the prayer: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, three times."
"18377","And he used to forbid gossip, and excessive asking, and wasting wealth, and withholding and demanding, and disobedience to mothers, and burying daughters alive."
"18378","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father."
"18379","And from Ibn Sirin, he raised it to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he nudged my back or my shoulder with something that was with him, he said: And I followed him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, relieved himself, then he came and said: Have you water with you, I said: Yes, and with me is a flat skin of water, and he washed his face, and upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, so he put his hand in and raised the cloak upon his shoulder, and took out his hands from beneath the cloak, and washed his forearms and wiped over the turban, he said: And he mentioned the forelock with something, and wiped over his two leather socks, then we came forward and caught the people in the dawn prayer, and Abd al-Rahman was leading them, and they had prayed one rakah, so I went to inform him, and he forbade me, so we prayed one rakah with him, and we made up what we had been preceded in."
"18380","Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from the hadith of Abbad ibn Ziyad, that Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah informed him that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah informed him that he raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the expedition of Tabuk, al-Mughirah said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to relieve himself before the privy, and I carried with him a water vessel before the dawn prayer, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned to me, I began pouring upon his hands from the vessel, and he washed his hands three times, then he washed his face, then he went to take out his cloak from his forearms, and the sleeves of his cloak were tight, so he put his hands into the cloak until he took out his forearms from beneath the cloak, and washed his forearms to the elbows, then he wiped over his two leather socks, then he came forward, al-Mughirah said: So I came forward with him until we found the people having put Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf forward praying with them, and he caught one of the two rakahs, Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: So he prayed with the people the last rakah, and when Abd al-Rahman gave the greeting, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood completing his prayer, and that alarmed the Muslims and they increased glorification, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his prayer, he turned to them, then he said: You did well, or: You were right, congratulating them that they prayed the prayer at its time."
"18381","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah, similar to the hadith of Abbad, al-Mughirah said: And I wanted to delay Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave him."
"18382","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night on a march, and he said: Have you water with you, I said: Yes, so he dismounted from his mount, then he walked until he disappeared from me in the darkness of the night, then he came, and I poured upon him from the water vessel, and he washed his face, and upon him was a wool cloak with narrow sleeves, and he could not take out his forearms from it, so he took them out from beneath the cloak, and he washed his forearms and wiped his head, then I bent down to remove his two leather socks, so he said: Leave them, for indeed I put them on pure, so he wiped over them."
"18383","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Thawr narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from the secretary of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution and wiped the bottom of the leather sock and its top."
"18384","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood until his feet swelled, so it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin, so he said: Shall I not be a thankful servant."
"18385","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdah and Abd al-Malik, they heard Warrad, he wrote to him, meaning al-Mughirah, Muawiyah wrote to him: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he wrote to him, meaning al-Mughirah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable."
"18386","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from al-Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has not relied who seeks incantation and is cauterized, and Sufyan said twice: Or is cauterized."
"18387","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mentioning it, from Simak, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Najran, he said: So they said: Have you seen what you recite: O sister of Harun, while Musa was before Isa by such and such, he said: So I returned and mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Did you not inform them that they used to name themselves after the prophets and the righteous before them."
"18388","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd, he said: I heard Ali ibn Rabiah, he said: I witnessed al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah go out one day and ascend the pulpit, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then he said: What is with this wailing in Islam, and a man of the Ansar had died and wailing was done over him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Lying upon me is not like lying upon anyone, so whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"18389","I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever is wailed over is punished for what he is wailed over."
"18390","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will remain people of my nation dominant over the people until the command of Allah comes to them while they are dominant."
"18391","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to me, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said to me: No one asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the Dajjal more than I asked him, and he said to me: What harms you from him, he said: I said: They say that with him is a mountain of bread and a river of water, he said: He is more insignificant before Allah than that."
"18392","Waki narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I ate garlic, then I came to the prayer place of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I found him having preceded me by one rakah, and when he prayed I stood to make up, and he found the smell of garlic, and he said: Whoever eats this plant, let him not approach our mosque until its smell goes, he said: So when I finished the prayer I came to him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed I have an excuse, hand me your hand, he said: And I found him, by Allah, easy, so he handed me his hand, and I put it into my sleeve to my chest, and he found it bound, so he said: Indeed you have an excuse."
"18393","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution and wiped over the two socks and the two sandals."
"18394","Waki and Rawh said: Said ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Rawh said: Ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah, he said: My uncle Ziyad ibn Jubayr narrated to me, and Waki said: From Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The rider is behind the funeral, and the walker is where he wishes of it, and the child is prayed over."
"18395","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade insulting the dead."
"18396","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not insult the dead, lest you harm the living."
"18397","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard a man with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not insult the dead, lest you harm the living."
"18398","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever narrates a hadith while seeing it is a lie, he is one of the liars."
"18399","Waki narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Sakhrah Jami ibn Shaddad, from Mughirah ibn Abdullah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was a guest with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and he ordered a side, and it was roasted, he said: So he took the knife and began cutting for me from it, he said: Then Bilal came to inform him of the prayer, so he threw the knife and said: What is with him, may his hands be dusty, Mughirah said: And my mustache was long, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, trimmed it for me upon a toothstick, or he said: I will trim it for you upon a toothstick."
"18400","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab consulted the people concerning the miscarriage of the woman, he said: So al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judging concerning it with a ghurrah, a slave or a slavegirl, he said: So Umar said: Bring me one who testifies with you, he said: So Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified for him."
"18401","Waki narrated to us, Tamah ibn Amr al-Jafari narrated to us, from Umar ibn Bayan al-Taghlibi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah al-Thaqafi, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells wine, let him cut up the pigs, meaning cutting them in pieces."
"18402","Yazid informed us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Uqbah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take hold of the waist of Sufyan ibn Sahl al-Thaqafi and say: O Sufyan, do not let your lower garment hang down, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang down."
"18403","Yazid informed us, al-Masudi informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and stood up after the two rakahs, so we said Subhan Allah to him and he went on, and when he completed the prayer he made the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and on one occasion he said: those behind him said Subhan Allah to him, so he gestured that they should stand up."
"18404","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur who said: I heard Mujahid narrating, he said: Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah narrated a hadith to me, and when I left him I had not retained it well, so I returned to him with a companion of mine, and I met Hassan ibn Abi Wajzah coming out from him, and he said: What brings you, and I said: Such and such, so Hassan said: Aqqar narrated it to us, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: He has not placed his trust in Allah who uses cauterization and seeks ruqyah."
"18405","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day Ibrahim died, so the people said: It eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are a sign among the signs of Allah, they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, pray and supplicate Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"18406","Abu al-Walid and Affan both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated to us, Iyad narrated to us, from Suwayd ibn Sarhan, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food, then the prayer was called, so he stood up, and he had performed ablution before that, so I brought him water to perform ablution from it, and he rebuked me and said: Put it behind you, and that, by Allah, grieved me, then he prayed, so I complained of that to Umar, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, al-Mughirah was distressed by your rebuking him and feared there might be something against him in your heart, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing against him in my heart except good, but he brought me water to perform ablution, while I had only eaten food, and had I done it the people after me would do it."
"18407","Waki narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Amir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Num, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he relieved himself, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot, he said: Rather you forgot, with this my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me."
"18408","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is cauterized or seeks ruqyah has disowned trust in Allah."
"18409","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the noon or afternoon prayer and stood up, so we said Subhan Allah, and he said Subhan Allah and gestured with his hand, meaning stand up, so we stood up, and when he finished his prayer he made two prostrations, then said: If one of you remembers before standing fully upright, let him sit down, and if he stands fully upright, let him not sit down."
"18410","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you stands up and has not stood fully upright, let him sit down, and if he has stood fully upright, let him not sit down, and let him make the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"18411","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hashim, meaning Ibn Hashim, narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a standing place and informed us of what will be in his nation until the Day of Resurrection, whoever retained it retained it, and whoever forgot it forgot it."
"18412","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me for water, so I came to a tent in which there was a Bedouin woman, and I said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he wants water to perform ablution, do you have any water, she said: May my father and mother be ransom for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by Allah no soul that the sky shades or the earth carries is more beloved to me than his soul, nor more honored, but this water skin is the skin of a dead animal, and I do not wish to defile the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it, so I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Return to her, for if she tanned it then that is its purification, so I returned to her and mentioned that to her, and she said: Yes, by Allah, I did tan it, so I brought him water from it, and on that day he was wearing a Syrian cloak and leather socks and a head cover, and he put his hands in from beneath the cloak, because of the narrowness of its sleeves, and performed ablution and wiped over the head cover and the leather socks."
"18413","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father al-Mughirah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, then came back, and I poured water over him, so he washed his face, then went to wash his forearms but the sleeve of the cloak was too tight for them, so he took them out from beneath the cloak and washed them, then wiped over his leather socks."
"18414","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, Yunus ibn al-Harith al-Taifi narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, or liked to pray, upon a tanned fur."
"18415","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from Urwah who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the tops of the leather socks."
"18416","Surayj and al-Hashimi also narrated it to us."
"18417","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Sharik, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, informed me that he heard Aba al-Saib, the freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, say: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shubah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out on a journey and stopped at a resting place, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, so I followed him with a water vessel and poured over him, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"18418","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Warrad, the freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of idle gossip, and withholding and demanding, and burying daughters alive, and disobedience to mothers, and wasting wealth."
"18419","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Jabir al-Jufi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl who said: I heard him narrating from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah that he stood up after the two rakahs and the people said Subhan Allah, and I think he said Subhan Allah and went on, then made two prostrations after he gave the salutation, and said: This is what we did with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that he had doubt about the word said Subhan Allah."
"18420","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Shibl narrated to us, from Amir, from Warrad, the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: Muawiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shubah: Write to me what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so al-Mughirah called me and wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when he finished the prayer: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things, O Allah, none can prevent what You give, and none can give what You prevent, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail him against You."
"18421","And I heard him forbidding idle gossip, and much asking, and wasting wealth, and burying daughters alive, and disobedience to mothers, and withholding and demanding."
"18422","Ali narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abdah, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he gave the salutation he said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things, O Allah, none can prevent what You give, and none can give what You prevent, like the hadith of al-Mughirah, except that he did not mention burying daughters alive."
"18423","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Taymi narrated to us, from Bakr, from al-Hasan, from Ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his forelock and wiped over his leather socks and turban, Bakr said: And I heard it from Ibn al-Mughirah."
"18424","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from Amir who said: Urwah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, from his father who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night on a journey, and he said to me: Do you have water, I said: Yes, so he dismounted from his mount, then went away from me until he was hidden from me in the darkness of the night, and he was wearing a cloak, and he tried to take his hands out but could not take his hands out of it, so he took his hands out from beneath the cloak and washed his hands and wiped over his head, then I went to remove his leather socks, and he said: Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure, and he wiped over them."
"18425","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abi Sakhrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: I spent a night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered a side of meat and it was roasted, then he took the knife and began to cut pieces for me from it, then Bilal came to call him to prayer, so he threw down the knife and said: What is with him, may his hands be dusted, and my mustache had grown long, so he trimmed it for me against a tooth stick, or he said: I will trim it for you against a tooth stick."
"18426","Waki narrated to us, Said ibn Ubayd al-Tai and Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabiah al-Walibi who said: The first one over whom wailing was done in Kufah was Qarazah ibn Kab al-Ansari, so al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is wailed over will be punished for what is wailed over him on the Day of Resurrection."
"18427","Waki narrated to us, from Misar, and Sufyan, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled, so it was said to him, and he said: Shall I not be a grateful servant."
"18428","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a Roman cloak with narrow sleeves."
"18429","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: And Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a hadith while seeing it to be a lie is one of the liars, and Abd al-Rahman said: He is one of the great liars."
"18430","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it, he said: He is one of the liars."
"18431","Waki narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, I heard it from al-Shabi who said: Urwah ibn al-Mughirah attested to me on the authority of his father that his father attested to him on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was on a journey and he made his camel kneel and his companions made theirs kneel, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself, then came back, and I brought him a water vessel, and he was wearing a Roman cloak with narrow sleeves, and he tried to take his hands out but they were too tight, so he took them out from beneath the cloak, then I poured over him and he performed ablution, and when he reached the leather socks I bent down to remove them, and he said: No, for I put them on while they were pure, so he performed ablution and wiped over them, al-Shabi said: So Urwah attested to me on the authority of his father, and his father attested to him on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18432","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah who said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shubah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled, so it was said to him: Has Allah not forgiven you what went before of your sin and what will come after, he said: Shall I not be a grateful servant."
